text She won't see me anymore?
text Those words start to sink in and press down on me, like sand trickling from the ceiling.
text Kotomi stays silent while biting her lip and looking downward.
text I can tell just how serious Kotomi is.
text I have no idea what made her say this today.
text But if Kotomi has a goal, and she wants to achieve it by herself...
text I have no reason to deny her that.
text @[Tomoya]
text All right.
text @[Tomoya]
text If you insist, I won't see you again, either.
text I say that without looking Kotomi in the eye.
text I can feel my own words burying me alive.
text Maybe I was just careless and this was inevitable.
text This was a friendship between the school's top honor student and a delinquent.
text We never would have been a good match anyway.
text No, I shouldn't think of it like that.
text It was only for a short time, but I'll cherish these few days I've spent with Kotomi.
text @[Tomoya]
text You'll be okay without me.
text @[Tomoya]
text You're a hard worker, so you can be greater than anyone.
text I try to say that as cheerfully as possible.
text @[Tomoya]
text I'll walk you back to the usual spot.
text Kotomi quietly shakes her head.
